From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Let the cast's sink describe itself the way a device does

A bluetooth headphone on this machine carries a session priority of two
thousand and ten, says plainly that it is not virtual, and says what shape of
thing it is. The ordinary policy then ranks it, routes to it and moves
streams onto it without anybody writing a line of code for the occasion.

The sink a cast makes carried none of that. It had no priority at all, so it
could not be ranked, and it was left to whatever happened to notice a new
sink had appeared - something that is neither this program nor the session
manager, writing the default output directly into the shared metadata a
second after the sink shows up. Being chosen that way works and is nobody's
decision.

So it now describes itself. Two thousand is above every output built into
this machine, which are in the hundreds, and below the two thousand and ten
of a headphone, so a cast takes the sound away from the speakers and leaves
it with anyone wearing headphones. There is no driver priority because a
headphone has none.

What is deliberately not copied is the rest of what a headphone carries: the
smart filter, the loopback group it belongs to, the bluetooth interface
itself. Those describe a thing the bluetooth module builds around real
hardware rather than settings that would build one here, and claiming that
interface would send its policy hunting for a device that does not exist.

diff -ruN a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
--- a/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
+++ b/src/nd-pulseaudio.c
@@ -345,6 +345,32 @@
                                                    "rate=48000 "
                                                    "sink_properties=device.class=\"sound\" "
                                                    "device.icon_name=\"network-wireless\" "
+                                                   /* Described the way a headphone describes
+                                                    * itself, so the ordinary policy can rank and
+                                                    * route this like anything else. A sink that
+                                                    * says nothing is ranked by nothing and left to
+                                                    * whatever happens to notice it.
+                                                    *
+                                                    * Two thousand sits above every output built
+                                                    * into the machine, which are in the hundreds,
+                                                    * and just below the two thousand and ten a
+                                                    * bluetooth headphone carries. So a cast takes
+                                                    * the sound from the speakers, and does not take
+                                                    * it from somebody wearing headphones. There is
+                                                    * no driver priority because a headphone has
+                                                    * none either.
+                                                    *
+                                                    * What is not copied from a headphone is the
+                                                    * smart filter, the loopback group and the
+                                                    * bluetooth interface. Those describe something
+                                                    * the bluetooth module builds around a device
+                                                    * rather than settings that would build one
+                                                    * here, and claiming that interface would send
+                                                    * its policy looking for hardware that is not
+                                                    * there. */
+                                                   "node.virtual=false "
+                                                   "priority.session=2000 "
+                                                   "device.form_factor=\"tv\" "
                                                    "device.description=\"%s\"",
                                                    sink_name,
                                                    self->name);
